WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.325
Lesson 3.0.

00:00:02.325 --> 00:00:06.160
The Mastery Starter for Module 3: Lending and Leverage.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.964
By the end, you'll know the five

00:00:07.964 --> 00:00:10.096
words this module runs on, and exactly

00:00:10.096 --> 00:00:12.064
how to tell when you've mastered it.

00:00:13.364 --> 00:00:14.654
Here's the plan.

00:00:14.654 --> 00:00:18.737
First, the sixty-second version: how lending markets actually work,

00:00:18.737 --> 00:00:21.619
and the one hard rule borrowing comes with.

00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:23.296
Second, the five words you'll

00:00:23.296 --> 00:00:24.994
need, each one drawn out.

00:00:24.994 --> 00:00:27.409
Third, what to have ready before you start.

00:00:27.409 --> 00:00:29.862
Fourth, your first safe step: supplying a

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:32.264
small amount, with no borrowing yet.

00:00:32.264 --> 00:00:34.779
And finally, the mastery ladder, so you know

00:00:34.779 --> 00:00:37.349
exactly what finishing this module looks like.

00:00:38.649 --> 00:00:41.214
Here's the whole module in one sentence.

00:00:41.214 --> 00:00:43.969
Lending markets let you earn interest by lending

00:00:43.969 --> 00:00:46.387
your assets out, or let you borrow against

00:00:46.387 --> 00:00:49.274
what you already own, without ever selling it.

00:00:49.274 --> 00:00:52.368
Borrowing comes with exactly one hard rule, worth

00:00:52.368 --> 00:00:55.894
knowing before anything else: if your collateral's value

00:00:55.894 --> 00:00:58.740
falls too far, it gets sold automatically, at

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:01.339
a penalty, whether you're watching or not.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.960
Here's the mechanism underneath every lending market.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:09.210
Lenders deposit assets into a shared pool, and earn

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:12.885
interest, paid by whoever borrows from that same pool.

00:01:12.885 --> 00:01:16.015
Borrowers lock up collateral, worth more than what they

00:01:16.015 --> 00:01:19.110
borrow, and can borrow against it without selling.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.706
The interest rate itself moves with how much

00:01:21.706 --> 00:01:24.245
of the pool is currently borrowed, which is

00:01:24.245 --> 00:01:26.380
exactly word five, coming up shortly.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.015
This isn't a small corner of DeFi.

00:01:30.015 --> 00:01:34.171
Lending markets are consistently among the largest categories of

00:01:34.171 --> 00:01:37.624
value locked in the entire industry, because the core

00:01:37.624 --> 00:01:41.780
trade, earning yield, or unlocking liquidity without selling, is

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.510
useful in almost any market condition.

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:47.148
That's also exactly why the one hard rule

00:01:47.148 --> 00:01:49.473
matters so much: a lot of real value

00:01:49.473 --> 00:01:51.860
sits directly on the other side of it.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:54.935
Now, the five words you'll need.

00:01:56.235 --> 00:01:57.950
Word one: collateral.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.975
What you lock up in order to borrow.

00:01:59.975 --> 00:02:01.830
Here's the actual sequence.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.765
You deposit an asset you own, as collateral.

00:02:04.765 --> 00:02:07.021
The protocol values it, continuously,

00:02:07.021 --> 00:02:09.280
against the current market price.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:12.559
And it stays locked, entirely unavailable to you, for

00:02:12.559 --> 00:02:15.170
as long as your loan against it stays open.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:19.075
Word two: L.T.V., loan-to-value.

00:02:19.075 --> 00:02:21.970
Your debt, divided by your collateral's value.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:24.202
It's the single number that tells you how

00:02:24.202 --> 00:02:26.680
borrowed you actually are, at any moment.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:29.329
A lower L.T.V. means more room before

00:02:29.329 --> 00:02:31.929
trouble; a higher one means less.

00:02:31.929 --> 00:02:34.389
Every other safety number in this module,

00:02:34.389 --> 00:02:36.672
including word three, is really just a

00:02:36.672 --> 00:02:39.659
different way of expressing this same relationship.

00:02:40.959 --> 00:02:42.799
Word three: health factor.

00:02:42.799 --> 00:02:46.569
Your actual safety margin, expressed as a single number.

00:02:46.569 --> 00:02:48.844
Above one, your position is safe.

00:02:48.844 --> 00:02:51.849
At exactly one, it's at the liquidation line.

00:02:51.849 --> 00:02:55.949
Below one, liquidation can happen, automatically, without warning.

00:02:55.949 --> 00:02:58.960
Watch this chart as E.T.H.'s price moves: the

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:02.691
health factor tracks it directly, since collateral value

00:03:02.691 --> 00:03:05.244
is what the whole number is built from.

00:03:06.544 --> 00:03:08.454
Word four: liquidation.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:11.693
The forced, automatic sale of your collateral, to repay

00:03:11.693 --> 00:03:15.059
your debt, once your health factor crosses below one.

00:03:15.059 --> 00:03:17.102
It isn't a warning, and it isn't

00:03:17.102 --> 00:03:20.384
negotiable; it's code, executing exactly as written,

00:03:20.384 --> 00:03:23.099
the moment the number crosses the line.

00:03:23.099 --> 00:03:25.114
And in a fast, falling market, one

00:03:25.114 --> 00:03:28.164
liquidation can trigger selling pressure that pushes

00:03:28.164 --> 00:03:30.294
prices further down, triggering more.

00:03:31.594 --> 00:03:33.756
One quick, concrete number, so

00:03:33.756 --> 00:03:35.799
LTV isn't just a formula.

00:03:35.799 --> 00:03:42.511
Deposit $1,000 of collateral, borrow $400 against it, and

00:03:42.511 --> 00:03:47.324
your LTV is exactly 40%: $400 ÷ $1,000.

00:03:47.324 --> 00:03:50.160
Most protocols cap how high that ratio can

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:53.919
go before your position becomes eligible for liquidation.

00:03:55.219 --> 00:03:56.309
Quick check.

00:03:56.309 --> 00:03:58.027
What does a health factor below

00:03:58.027 --> 00:03:59.584
one actually mean, right now?

00:04:04.004 --> 00:04:08.164
The answer: liquidation can happen, automatically, without warning.

00:04:08.164 --> 00:04:09.580
It's not a soft warning

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:11.174
zone; it's the line itself.

00:04:12.474 --> 00:04:14.569
Word five: utilisation.

00:04:14.569 --> 00:04:16.166
How much of a lending pool's

00:04:16.166 --> 00:04:18.779
total deposits are currently borrowed out.

00:04:18.779 --> 00:04:20.804
Here's why it matters directly.

00:04:20.804 --> 00:04:23.740
Low utilisation means most of the pool sits

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.709
idle, so rates stay low, for both sides.

00:04:26.709 --> 00:04:30.232
As utilisation climbs toward full, rates rise, often

00:04:30.232 --> 00:04:33.023
sharply, to pull in more lenders and push

00:04:33.023 --> 00:04:36.014
out some borrowers, keeping the pool solvent.

00:04:37.314 --> 00:04:38.359
Before you start.

00:04:39.659 --> 00:04:42.119
Two things, both from earlier modules.

00:04:42.119 --> 00:04:45.196
First, Modules Zero through Two done: safe wallet

00:04:45.196 --> 00:04:48.519
habits, and comfort trading on-chain, since you'll be

00:04:48.519 --> 00:04:52.204
interacting with real lending contracts in this module.

00:04:52.204 --> 00:04:54.756
Second, comfort actually using a DEX on

00:04:54.756 --> 00:04:57.372
a low-fee network, since your first safe

00:04:57.372 --> 00:04:59.969
step needs no new skill beyond that.

00:04:59.969 --> 00:05:01.353
If either is missing, go

00:05:01.353 --> 00:05:02.904
back and finish those first.

00:05:04.204 --> 00:05:05.479
Your first safe step.

00:05:06.779 --> 00:05:08.439
Your first step in this module

00:05:08.439 --> 00:05:10.399
doesn't touch borrowing at all.

00:05:10.399 --> 00:05:12.851
Supply twenty dollars of U.S.D.C.

00:05:12.851 --> 00:05:15.314
to a blue-chip lending market.

00:05:15.314 --> 00:05:18.699
Read its utilisation, right there on the same screen.

00:05:18.699 --> 00:05:20.049
Then withdraw it.

00:05:20.049 --> 00:05:22.961
You're building the habit of reading a market's real

00:05:22.961 --> 00:05:25.544
state before you ever put real debt against it.

00:05:26.844 --> 00:05:28.529
Here's the worked example.

00:05:28.529 --> 00:05:31.499
Open a blue-chip lending market's supply screen.

00:05:31.499 --> 00:05:35.082
Deposit twenty dollars of U.S.D.C. Read the pool's

00:05:35.082 --> 00:05:38.824
current utilisation and supply rate, right there.

00:05:38.824 --> 00:05:41.249
Then withdraw the same twenty dollars.

00:05:41.249 --> 00:05:44.044
Small, reversible, and it teaches you exactly

00:05:44.044 --> 00:05:46.475
where to look before Lesson three point

00:05:46.475 --> 00:05:49.149
one asks you to actually calculate anything.

00:05:50.449 --> 00:05:52.890
One real number, so this module doesn't

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:55.204
feel like a niche corner of DeFi.

00:05:55.204 --> 00:05:58.410
Lending protocols have consistently held tens of

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:01.223
billions of dollars in total value locked,

00:06:01.223 --> 00:06:03.944
across major chains, year after year.

00:06:03.944 --> 00:06:08.523
This is outside research, not this program's own

00:06:08.523 --> 00:06:12.355
data, but it's exactly why the habits in

00:06:12.355 --> 00:06:15.439
this module matter at real scale.

00:06:16.739 --> 00:06:17.829
Quick check.

00:06:17.829 --> 00:06:19.698
Why does the first safe step in

00:06:19.698 --> 00:06:22.034
this module involve no borrowing at all?

00:06:26.454 --> 00:06:29.170
The answer: it builds the habit of reading

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:32.580
a lending market's real state, utilisation and rates,

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:35.169
before you ever put real debt against it.

00:06:36.469 --> 00:06:37.564
The mastery ladder.

00:06:38.864 --> 00:06:41.879
Here's how you'll measure your progress through Module Three.

00:06:41.879 --> 00:06:44.577
Beginner: supplies stablecoins, and reads

00:06:44.577 --> 00:06:47.189
utilisation and rates before acting.

00:06:47.189 --> 00:06:50.146
Practitioner: borrows with a health factor of two or

00:06:50.146 --> 00:06:53.179
higher, and keeps a written defence ladder ready.

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:56.391
And Master: runs correlated loops and perpetual

00:06:56.391 --> 00:07:00.138
futures positions, with computed liquidation prices and

00:07:00.138 --> 00:07:02.480
break-even rates, known in advance.

00:07:03.781 --> 00:07:06.381
Here's the road ahead, lesson by lesson.

00:07:06.381 --> 00:07:09.116
3.1, how lending markets work.

00:07:09.116 --> 00:07:12.131
3.2, health factor and liquidation.

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:14.506
3.3, leveraged loops.

00:07:14.506 --> 00:07:16.981
3.4, perpetual futures.

00:07:16.981 --> 00:07:19.109
And 3.5, CDPs and minting

00:07:19.109 --> 00:07:22.056
your own dollars against collateral.

00:07:23.356 --> 00:07:26.226
One more preview, from Lesson three point three.

00:07:26.226 --> 00:07:30.210
A leveraged loop, supplying, borrowing, and re-supplying the same

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:33.590
asset repeatedly, only works when the supply rate beats

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:36.486
the borrow rate; that spread is everything.

00:07:36.486 --> 00:07:39.151
Get the spread wrong, and leverage amplifies

00:07:39.151 --> 00:07:40.868
a loss exactly as fast as it

00:07:40.868 --> 00:07:42.526
would have amplified a gain.

00:07:43.826 --> 00:07:46.528
And one more preview, from Lesson three point

00:07:46.528 --> 00:07:48.766
five, the far end of this module.

00:07:48.766 --> 00:07:52.492
A C.D.P., a collateralised debt position, lets you mint

00:07:52.492 --> 00:07:57.017
your own stablecoin directly against locked collateral, rather than

00:07:57.017 --> 00:07:59.846
borrowing an existing one from a pool.

00:07:59.846 --> 00:08:02.405
Same core idea as everything else in this

00:08:02.405 --> 00:08:06.670
module, over-collateralise, respect the health-factor line, just with

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:09.351
a different destination for what you borrow.

00:08:10.651 --> 00:08:13.512
You've mastered this module when you can open a

00:08:13.512 --> 00:08:17.089
borrow, monitor it, and unwind it, without ever approaching

00:08:17.089 --> 00:08:20.846
liquidation, and without needing to check on it anxiously.

00:08:20.846 --> 00:08:22.511
Not a large position.

00:08:22.511 --> 00:08:25.348
A repeatable, controlled process, with a defence

00:08:25.348 --> 00:08:27.491
plan written down before you need it.

00:08:28.791 --> 00:08:29.831
One more.

00:08:29.831 --> 00:08:32.801
Your health factor is currently one point three, and

00:08:32.801 --> 00:08:35.846
falling steadily as the market moves against you.

00:08:35.846 --> 00:08:37.831
What's the actual state of your position?

00:08:42.251 --> 00:08:44.417
The answer: still above the liquidation

00:08:44.417 --> 00:08:46.341
line, but with shrinking room.

00:08:46.341 --> 00:08:48.510
This is exactly when a written defence

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:50.401
ladder tells you what to do next,

00:08:50.401 --> 00:08:52.626
not the moment to decide under pressure.

00:08:53.926 --> 00:08:55.111
Last check.

00:08:55.111 --> 00:08:57.926
What does mastering Module Three actually look like?

00:09:02.346 --> 00:09:05.567
The answer: opening, monitoring and unwinding a

00:09:05.567 --> 00:09:09.460
borrow without ever approaching liquidation, a repeatable

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:11.406
process, not a lucky outcome.

00:09:12.706 --> 00:09:15.712
One honest note before the recap, since leverage

00:09:15.712 --> 00:09:18.165
and perpetual futures sit at the top of

00:09:18.165 --> 00:09:20.551
this module's ladder for a reason.

00:09:20.551 --> 00:09:24.070
Everything in this module works both directions: the

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:27.788
same borrowing mechanism that lets you unlock liquidity

00:09:27.788 --> 00:09:30.643
without selling can amplify a loss just as

00:09:30.643 --> 00:09:33.731
fast as a gain, once leverage is involved.

00:09:33.731 --> 00:09:36.676
Master the beginner and practitioner rungs first.

00:09:36.676 --> 00:09:38.321
There's no shortcut past them.

00:09:39.621 --> 00:09:41.576
Let's recap the five words.

00:09:41.576 --> 00:09:44.856
Collateral: what you lock up, valued continuously.

00:09:44.856 --> 00:09:48.956
L.T.V.: debt over collateral value, how borrowed you are.

00:09:48.956 --> 00:09:53.191
Health factor: your safety margin; below one means liquidation.

00:09:53.191 --> 00:09:56.256
Liquidation: automatic, forced, no warning.

00:09:56.256 --> 00:09:58.602
And utilisation: how full a pool is,

00:09:58.602 --> 00:10:00.757
and exactly what drives its rates.

00:10:02.057 --> 00:10:03.752
That's the Mastery Starter.

00:10:03.752 --> 00:10:05.898
You now have the whole module in your

00:10:05.898 --> 00:10:08.665
head: why lending markets exist, the five words,

00:10:08.665 --> 00:10:11.037
your first safe step, and the ladder that

00:10:11.037 --> 00:10:12.862
tells you when you're done.

00:10:12.862 --> 00:10:16.357
Next up, Lesson 3.1: How lending markets work.
